From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Subject: [PATCH] ath11k: do not clean up a kicked-out peer under base_lock

ath11k_peer_sta_kickout_event() called ath11k_dp_peer_cleanup(), which
takes base_lock itself, with base_lock held, so the spurious kickout
branch spun on its own lock. Drop the lock before the cleanup, keeping
the vdev_id read under it, and initialise save_peer and sta, which are
otherwise unset when no radio holds the peer.

Taken from the 999-900 update in JuliusBairaktaris/openwrt-nss-edma
(fe08e746309) and carried as a separate patch on our backports 6.18.26
series.

Link: https://github.com/qosmio/openwrt-ipq/pull/111
Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/wmi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/wmi.c
@@ -8067,11 +8067,11 @@ static void ath11k_scan_event(struct ath
 static void ath11k_peer_sta_kickout_event(struct ath11k_base *ab, struct sk_buff *skb)
 {
 	struct wmi_peer_sta_kickout_arg arg = {};
-	struct ieee80211_sta *sta;
+	struct ieee80211_sta *sta = NULL;
 	struct ath11k_peer *peer;
-	struct ath11k_peer *save_peer;
+	struct ath11k_peer *save_peer = NULL;
 	struct ath11k *ar;
 	struct ath11k *save_ar;
 	int i;
 
 	if (ath11k_pull_peer_sta_kickout_ev(ab, skb, &arg) != 0) {
@@ -8102,11 +8102,15 @@ static void ath11k_peer_sta_kickout_even
 		ieee80211_report_low_ack(sta, 10);
 	}
 	if (!sta && save_peer) {
+		int vdev_id = save_peer->vdev_id;
+
+		spin_unlock_bh(&ab->base_lock);
 		ath11k_warn(ab, "Spurious quick kickout for STA %pM but found in peer table\n", arg.mac_addr);
-		ath11k_dp_peer_cleanup(save_ar, save_peer->vdev_id, arg.mac_addr);
+		ath11k_dp_peer_cleanup(save_ar, vdev_id, arg.mac_addr);
+	} else {
+		spin_unlock_bh(&ab->base_lock);
 	}
 
-	spin_unlock_bh(&ab->base_lock);
 	rcu_read_unlock();
 }
 
